   "fix": "Drop `private` and relocate both to the `Matrix` namespace at their canonical home (e.g. alongside `Matrix.norm_trace_le_card_of_mem_unitaryGroup` under `EpsilonEridani/Mathematics/DataStructures/Matrix/`), as `Matrix.sum_norm_sq_one_row` / `Matrix.sum_norm_sq_one_col`, and import them here.",
   "issue": "`private theorem sum_norm_sq_one_row` (line 251) and `private theorem sum_norm_sq_one_col` (line 255) are general infrastructure: their statements mention only `Matrix`, `\u2102` and `\u2016\u00b7\u2016`, and their proofs (`simp [Matrix.one_apply, apply_ite ...]`) do not touch the file's subject. Hiding them leaves the public hypotheses `hrow`/`hcol` of the ten `*_of_sum_norm_sq_eq_one` lemmas undischargeable at `V = 1` by any exported lemma \u2014 only the four `*_one` lemmas are given, so a user of `f2CCMinusLO_add_xf3CCMinusLO_eq_of_sum_norm_sq_eq_one` (line 333), `f2CCMinusLO_sub_f2CCPlusLO_eq_of_sum_norm_sq_eq_one` (line 439), `xf3CCMinusLO_add_xf3CCPlusLO_eq_of_sum_norm_sq_eq_one` (line 450) or `f2CCMinusLO_add_f2CCPlusLO_eq_two_mul_f2LO` (line 477) must reprove them.",
   "line": 251
  }
 ],
